-- title:
--   Controlled shift of one field (block rotation)
-- statement:
--   **Controlled shift of one field (block rotation).**  With the array `xs` (shape `[P, Q, B]`) on stack `0`, `P, Q, B` on stacks `1, 2, 4` and the offsets `a_0, …, a_{P-1}` (`a_p ≤ Q`) on stack `14`, `rotP` replaces `xs` by `pull [P, Q, B] [P, Q, B] (rotAddr Q as) 0 xs` (record `y` of block `p` moves to `(y + a_p) mod Q`), pops the offsets and restores every other stack; cost `O((V + 1)(Bb + 2) + (Bb + 2)^2)`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KILRot`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KIL.rotP_spec (t : IState HS) (xs : List ℤ) (as : ℕ → ℕ) (P Q B Bb : ℕ)
--       (R L1 L2 L4 L14 : List Item) (has : ∀ p, as p ≤ Q)
--       (hlen : xs.length = P * Q * B) (hb : Bnd Bb xs) (hB1 : 1 ≤ B) (hQ1 : 1 ≤ Q) (hP1 : 1 ≤ P)
--       (hV : zsz ((P * (Q * B) : ℕ) : ℤ) ≤ Bb)
--       (h0 : t.G 0 = ints xs ++ R) (h1 : t.G 1 = .int P :: L1) (h2 : t.G 2 = .int Q :: L2)
--       (h4 : t.G 4 = .int B :: L4)
--       (h14 : t.G 14 = ints ((List.range P).map fun p => (as p : ℤ)) ++ L14) :
--       rotP.ok t ∧ rotP.run t =
--           (t.upd 0 (ints (AModel.pull [P, Q, B] [P, Q, B] (rotAddr Q as) 0 xs) ++ R)).upd 14 L14 ∧
--         rotP.cost t ≤ 200000 * (P * (Q * B) + 1) * (Bb + 2) + 10 ^ 8 * (Bb + 2) ^ 2
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *Primitive (d): controlled shift as a rotation of blocks*: `rotP` reads an array on `[P, Q, B]` (stack `0`) and a list of offsets `a_p < Q` (stack `14`,
--   consumed) and rotates the `Q` records of block `p` cyclically by `a_p`:
--   record `y` of block `p` moves to `(y + a_p) mod Q`.  Cost `O(V + P · Q)` item operations.
--
